    "durationMs": 69802,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete and fully tested. Summary of what I built:\n\n- **Stack**: Express 5.3.0 + Knex/pg (migrations + query builder), database config read from `DATABASE_URL` (fails fast if unset).\n- **Files**: `knexfile.js`, `migrations/20261121000000_create_links.js` (links table with unique `code`, `clicks` counter), `db.js`, `app.js` (routes), `server.js` (binds `0.0.0.0:8000`), `start.sh` (runs pending migrations, then `exec node server.js` in foreground), README with startup instructions.\n- **Behavior verified end-to-end with curl**:\n  - `POST /links` → 201 `{\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\":0}` with the submitted URL returned unchanged; auto-generated 8-char codes; duplicate custom code → 409.\n  - 422 JSON errors for malformed JSON, missing/non-absolute/wrong-scheme URLs, and codes failing `[A-Za-z0-9_-]{4,20}`.\n  - `GET /links/{code}` → 200 / 404; `GET /r/{code}` → 302 with correct `Location`, incrementing clicks exactly once per hit via a single atomic `UPDATE ... RETURNING`; `GET /links` → ascending order with `total`.\n  - Restarted the server: links and click counts persisted through PostgreSQL; migrations re-ran as a no-op.\n\nTest data was cleaned up and the dev server stopped, so the API is ready to be launched with `sh start.sh`."
